  logs, so the timeline the checker used to decide is also the one the reader
  sees.
- [x] **Rendering.** Pretty output right-aligns line numbers, trims source to
  48 columns and labels to 60, and prints `file:line:col` for steps in another
  module. `--ascii` swaps `①`/`▸`/`◂ here`/`…` for ASCII; colour is a terminal
  decoration switched off by `--no-color` or `NO_COLOR`.
- [x] **Cascade control and fixes.** Type errors still suppress ownership
  analysis at the driver gate. Repeated uses of a moved place now fold into
  one report as `also used at lines …`. Diagnostics sort by primary location;
  5 stops / 10 warns are shown unless `--all` is passed. Every STOP is made
  through `fmt::make`, which attaches a code-specific `try:` fix.
- [x] **Explain corpus.** Every code listed in §16.10 has a complete
  WHAT/WHY/BAD/GOOD/NOTE/SEE lesson. Pages harmony-base already printed stay
  byte-identical for the driver differential gate. `tests/harmony-final/diag.sh`
  is the new UX gate (16 checks) and runs from `make test`.

### Final library, tooling and test sweep [x]

- [x] **Formatter.** `harmony fmt` prints one canonical token-based style with
  four-space indentation, preserved comments and stable generic spacing. The
